    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Letting y be the value of the underlying variable (the liability), the observed phenotypic value z can be regarded as a function of the liability, $ z = \\phi(y) $, where $ \\phi $ is the developmental map that rescales the underlying liability value y into the phenotypic value z. For a simple threshold character, letting $ y_c $ be the critical value, and denoting the alternate character states by 0 and 1,",
