          142.0,
          977.0,
          1106.0,
          1335.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "9d25ce50ff49f3a0732138423730ff3e960c597a866a45a8d1c6a6e44ac22e45"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Suppose the character of interest has $k$ discrete states, which we order from 1 to $k$. Let $q(m)$ be the cumulative frequency to (and including) class $m$, and define $x_m = \\text{prb}[q(m)]$ to be the probit-scale value associated with $q(m)$, i.e., $x_m$ satisfies $\\Pr(U \\leq x_m) = q(m)$ where $U$ is a unit normal. The width of liability values that map to class $m$ is estimated by",
      "source_page": 324,
      "printed_page": 304,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter11:p018:b10"
