    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where the units of $ D_m $ are in terms of number of standard deviations of liability values (Figure 11.9). Since $ q(k) = 1 $ and $ q(0) = 0 $, the widths for the first and last classes are not defined, as $ \\text{prb}[1] = -\\text{prb}[0] = \\infty $. Using standard results (Kendall and Stuart 1977, p. 254), the sampling variance for the estimator $ D_m $ is given by",
