    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "yielding a standard error of $ \\sqrt{0.096} = 0.31 $ and an estimated width of liability values mapping to the four-bristle class as $ 6.44\\sigma \\pm 0.31\\sigma $. Sheldon et al. found considerable variation in the strength of canalization across isogenic lines. The mean $ D_4 $ of all lines was 5.39, but ranged from $ 6.44 \\pm 0.31 $ down to $ 3.34 \\pm 0.10 $.",
      "source_page": 327,
      "printed_page": 307,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_chapter11:p021:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
